# 8.2.diagnosis.superposition.eliminated.stone

## .what

state the **eliminated set** — the scenarios ruled out, and for each, the **specific test result**
that eliminated it. this is the audit trail of the collapse: it proves each drop was earned by
evidence, never by low probability alone.

## .inputs

- `4.3.scenario.elimination.assay.plan.yield.md` — the result → elimination map
- `2.3.scenario.enumeration.blend.yield.md` — the full enumerated set (to show what was dropped)

## .do

- list each eliminated scenario with the **assay result** that ruled it out (per the phase-4 map) —
  "test X came back Y, which eliminates Z"
- state plainly which scenarios remain **un-eliminated but low-rank** — these are NOT eliminated; they
  stay in the live set (8.1), covered by the acuity envelope (phase 7) and the veto (phase 9)
- name the **irreducible set** — the scenarios that stay live if every assay is inconclusive

## .emit

into `8.2.diagnosis.superposition.eliminated.yield.md` — the eliminated set with per-scenario
evidence, and the irreducible-if-inconclusive set.

## .done when

every eliminated scenario cites the test result that ruled it out, no scenario is dropped on low
probability alone, and the irreducible set is named.
